    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TDvuJ2KygqHcBPtkDgePBK)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-reading-refresh` failed with `Can't get uuid of {content id … of database id 2 …}` (error -1728): AppleScript's `uuid of every item of <search result>` does not read the fields of a list of records.\n- The listing is now JavaScript for Automation (`sp-reading--jxa`), reading `uuid` and `name` of all records of the database in bulk and keeping the names ending in `.pdf`. This is the same call pattern `tools/devonthink-to-litdb.py` already uses on your Mac.\n- The same fix is in the stacked PRs #415 (browser listing) and #418 (search, similar, preview), merged up through #421. The other AppleScript (tags, `path of`, store link, probes) is still untried.\n- Docs: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-reading.org` and the tangled `sp-reading.el`; one new ERT test checks the script text and that refresh parses its output.\n\n## Not tested\n- The script on the Mac (I cannot run DEVONthink). 8 ERT tests of `sp-reading` pass with the output faked.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 422-sp-reading-listing-script; git checkout 422-sp-reading-listing-script`, restart Emacs.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-reading-refresh` → message \"sp-reading: N PDFs in literature\" (N about 15,000), no long dump. It may take a few seconds.\n- [ ] `M-:` `(gethash \"harrison-2010-therborn-post-marx\" sp-reading-index)` → a UUID string.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-reading-open`, choose a key → the record opens in DEVONthink.\n- [ ] If it still fails, paste the first 300 characters of the error.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC\n",
    "changed_files": 3,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-12T22:49:59Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check is red here, and on `main` too, so it is not caused by this PR. The failing module is `sp-litnotes-titles.el`: commit 87a4fbb7 (\"Add ` (ed.)` suffix by hand\") changed the `.el` without the doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-titles.org`. This PR's own files tangle cleanly. The same failure shows on the stacked PRs (#415 onward) until `main` is fixed; I have not touched that module.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
